    {
      "id": "figure-4",
      "stableKey": "p14:figure:Figure 4: Another example HotpotQA question, where the original label is outdate",
      "kind": "image",
      "section": "figure",
      "page": 14,
      "pageIndex": 13,
      "bbox": {
        "x": 0.17647058823529413,
        "y": 0.42960226656210543,
        "w": 0.6486928104575164,
        "h": 0.36964015768031877
      },
      "score": 0.9180853366851807,
      "title": "Figure 4: Another example HotpotQA question, where the original label is outdated. Only ReAct is able to obtain the up-to-date answer thanks to real-world web interaction plus reasoning. During trajectory inspection, we also find that sometimes ReAct does not agree with dataset labels as the labels themselves could be outdated. For example, as shown in Figure 4, the question asks about the size of a hotel, which increased from the HotpotQA construction time. While Standard and CoT give wrong answers due to hallucination, Act fails despite the access of real-world web interaction, due to a lack of reasoning to guide how to interact with the Internet for QA. Only ReAct is able to retrieve up-to-date information from the Internet and provide a reasonable answer. Therefore, better incorporation of reasoning abilities might benefit recent Internet-augmented language models (Nakano et al., 2021; Lazaridou et al., 2022; Shuster et al., 2022a) for up-to-date task solving.",
      "layoutRegionId": "ffbbf434-0975-49d2-a13b-4e5da8c438c6"
    },
    {
      "id": "figure-5",
      "stableKey": "p15:figure:Figure 5: A human-in-the-loop behavior correction example with ReAct in AlfWorld",
      "kind": "image",
      "section": "figure",
